      "side": 1,
      "message": "this the right idea of what we want to do in terms of program executions.\n\nInstead of forking in this code, let\u0027s take one of two paths\n\n1) not include i2c_master.c at all in the zephyr build and have the i2c shim provide these i2c_read and i2c_write interfaces.\n2) include the i2c_master.c file and just shim at the `chip_i2c_xfer` level and have the shim provide that function, which would then be implemented with zephyr APIs\n\nNote I think option 1 will be easier since there are less dependencies there.\n\nEither options though we will need to track that we are including some i2c unwedging/recovery support. I can\u0027t remember if Zephyr already provides this or not.\n\nWe also need to ensure that multiple tasks/threads are serialized when the call into i2c_read APIs. I don\u0027t know if Zephyr does this already or not either.",
